 "verdict": "THE REGISTERED CRITERIA FAIL: the world is *nearly* a cluster, and where it stops being one the reason is the position, not noise. In design groups with identical parameters, 44 of 841 worlds that received two or more seeds disagree in outcome (0.052, Wilson [0.0392, 0.0695]) - below the registered 10 % and only 2.149x the beta-binomial prediction at ICC = 0.955 (registered: >= 3x). The ICC refitted on this pool is 0.9816 (95 % interval [0.6698, 0.6906] around the sigma profile mode; the joint sigma puts it higher), so X199's 0.955 is not overturned: on a pool with many repeats the label predicts a lot. What the clone pairs do expose is the other half of R4: 42 of 736 at F=0.03 steps=400, 2 of 40 at F=0.03 steps=2000, i.e. almost all disagreement sits in the arrays where two seeds of one phase are far apart in the domain. The descriptive check agrees: the median distance difference to the nearest edge is 6.0 cells in a disagreeing world against 0 in an agreeing one, and only 0.0227 of the disagreeing worlds have both runs at the same edge distance. So the label (cell, phase) is not a sufficient statistic for the world: it fixes the local inflow and leaves the distance to the boundary free, and that free coordinate moves the outcome. C1-C3: partly hold: C3_icc_refitted_on_p1."
}
